<metadata><name>Circle Lake Trail</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:249-3: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.405262" lon="-121.861126"><ele>1458.1</ele><name>Ray Benson Sno-park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:ray-benson-sno-park (OSM way 205969667); confidence: high; pdf_page: 250; quote: From Ray Benson Sno-Park ski northwest (clockwise) through mixed forest to the north leg</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.418796" lon="-121.842073"><ele>1472.8</ele><name>North Loop NE corner, Circle Lake Trail start</name><desc>source: OSM node 8308019839, North Loop / Circle Lake Ski Trail junction; confidence: high; pdf_page: 251; quote: The trail starts at the northeast corner of the North Loop and is best reached by skiing the west and north legs of the North Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.400126" lon="-121.821311"><ele>1426.5</ele><name>Island Junction Shelter (knoll)</name><desc>source: OSM end of Island Junction Ski Trail (way 893879427), the spur off the Circle Lake Ski Trail; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 251; quote: At the junction, turn southwest and ski 100 yards on the Circle Lake Trail and then to the off-trail knoll where the Island Junction Shelter is sited</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.394592" lon="-121.839752"><ele>1443.2</ele><name>Circle Lake Trail joins the South Loop</name><desc>source: OSM node 7675748822, Circle Lake / South Loop / Two Buttes Cutoff ski trails; confidence: high; pdf_page: 251; quote: From the shelter, ski the trail southwest as it climbs to join the South Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.405262" lon="-121.861126"><ele>1458.1</ele><name>Ray Benson Sno-park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:ray-benson-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 251; quote: The South Loop-Circle Lake Trail crosses the South Loop from east to west, cutting it into a shorter loop</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Circle Lake Trail</name><desc>1. Ray Benson Sno-park -&gt; North Loop NE corner, Circle Lake Trail start: osm (high), 1.87 mi | 2. North Loop NE corner, Circle Lake Trail start -&gt; Island Junction Shelter (knoll): osm (high), 2.39 mi | 3. Island Junction Shelter (knoll) -&gt; Circle Lake Trail joins the South Loop: osm (high), 1.03 mi | 4. Circle Lake Trail joins the South Loop -&gt; Ray Benson Sno-park: osm (medium), 1.97 mi</desc>
